{
  "summary": "Passes base32 I2P addresses directly to the SAM `STREAM CONNECT` command instead of executing a separate `NAMING LOOKUP` command first. This eliminates an unnecessary round trip to the local I2P SAM proxy on every outbound I2P connection.",
  "problem": "Outbound I2P connections incur latency from a redundant `NAMING LOOKUP` step before connecting. When a peer cannot be resolved during lookup, the SAM proxy returns an empty value that Bitcoin Core treats as a proxy error rather than a peer failure, preventing AddrMan from properly recording the failed attempt.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'As the SAM protocol accepts a `.b32.i2p` address as the `DESTINATION` parameter for the `STREAM CONNECT` command, the `NAMING LOOKUP` round trip can be skipped on every outbound connection.'",
    "PR description: 'This should ostensibly make failure handling more accurate in certain situations as well, since a peer that cannot be resolved now returns `CANT_REACH_PEER`/`TIMEOUT` rather than there being an empty `VALUE=` key in the lookup reply. A missing `VALUE=` is a proxy error, so the attempt isn't recorded in AddrMan.'"
